{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-core":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-core/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/sec-stochastic-mechanics-orphan-reconnect-intro","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Prose","doco:Section"],"label":"sec:stochastic-mechanics-orphan-reconnect-intro","kind":"prose","text":"stochastic-mechanics-orphan-reconnect-intro.md","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"sec:stochastic-mechanics-orphan-reconnect-intro\"></a><p>The <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q</code>-machinery has two degenerate limits, and this section takes both. At <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q \\to 1</code> the Lusztig canonical basis recovers the classical basis; at <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q \\to \\infty</code> the reverse limit strips the deformation from the other side. The <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\Phi_q</code> / <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">A_J</code> identification is what connects the two, and is treated between them.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/stochastic-mechanics-orphan-reconnect-intro.md","heading":"","page":"b/sec-stochastic-mechanics-orphan-reconnect-intro","qa":{"counts":{"pass":57,"fail":0,"warn":0,"na":18,"unknown":0,"stale":0},"milnor":{"total":2,"notPassing":0}}}
